what: the SDK by `brew install --cask android-commandlinetools` +
  sdkmanager (platform-tools, platforms;android-35, build-tools) into
  ~/Library/Android/sdk; okay-compose/app becomes a Kotlin
  Multiplatform module with a desktop and an Android target sharing
  Render.kt/Client.kt; a debug APK built by Gradle. Running it needs
  an emulator image (a further download) — built is the claim, run is
  reported as it is.

predict: the SDK download and the Android Gradle plugin are the
  heaviest things this session has run; the box's memory decides.
